    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I changed:\n\n## Changes\n\n**Behaviour** \u2014 replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133): start at 1, +1 when an email is present, +1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3 (4 reserved for tenure). The old logic's `householdSize`/`GOLD` branch is gone, since level 4 is reserved.\n\n1. **`util/MembershipLevels.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility helper, `MembershipLevels.of(Owner)`, holding the level rule. This mirrors the existing `CityRegions` util pattern and gives the two consumers (mapper + audit) one shared source instead of duplicated logic.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 renamed the `membershipTier` schema property to `membershipLevel` (type `integer`, `int32`, `min 1`/`max 3`), which regenerates the `OwnerDto` field. The old string field is removed from the response.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `@Mapping` now targets `membershipLevel`, delegating through a thin default method to `MembershipLevels.of(owner)` (keeping the util reference inside the interface, consistent with how `locality`/`CityRegions` works \u2014 a direct qualified expression would fail to compile in the generated impl for lack of an import).\n\n4. **`function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel=` (using the same helper) in place of the old tier.\n\n5. **`function/owner/CountHouseholdMembers.java`** \u2014 corrected the now-stale javadoc that claimed household size \"drives the membership tier.\"\n\nTest result: `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` passes (a unique owner with an email \u2192 `membershipLevel` = 3), and the audit log confirms `membershipLevel=3`. `BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures.",
